<p>Prebuilt Python wheels also exist for Linux aarch64.</p><br>

<b id="quickstart">Quick start (Python)</b>

<p>Install the package from PyPI:</p>

<pre>
pip install quadriga-lib
</pre>

<p>Create a 2 × 2 3GPP antenna array at 3.7 GHz and print the directivity of its first element (about 9.8 dBi):</p>

<pre>
import quadriga_lib

ant = quadriga_lib.arrayant.generate('3gpp', M=2, N=2, freq=3.7e9)
print(quadriga_lib.version())
print(quadriga_lib.arrayant.calc_directivity(ant, 0))
</pre>

<p>The same example for MATLAB, Octave and C++ is on the <a href="download.html">download page</a>.
The <a href="python_api.html">Python</a>, <a href="mex_api.html">MATLAB / Octave</a> and <a href="cpp_api.html">C++</a>
API references have more examples.</p><br>

